# The build context is sent to the daemon in full before anything runs, so
# this is about build time as much as image contents.
.git
.venv
data
.claude
tests
docs
.github
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
*.iccase
# The ui build stage needs ui/ sources only; these three are regenerated
# inside the stage or not needed, and node_modules alone is hundreds of MB
# of context upload. Excluding ui/dist also means the stage can never COPY a
# stale host build over its own output.
# The workspace root's tree, which one `npm ci` fills for both packages.
node_modules
ui/node_modules
ui/dist
ui/storybook-static
ui/.dev-root
e2e
# The same three for `server/`, which `docker/app/Dockerfile` builds from this same
# context. **`server/.tls` is the one that matters**: it holds a generated
# private key, and a context that carries it puts the key one careless `COPY
# server/ ./` away from the image. The other two are size and staleness --
# `server/dist` copied from the host would let an image ship a build older than
# its sources, which is the defect the ui/dist line above already records.
server/node_modules
server/dist
server/.tls
server/test-results
server/playwright-report
